On 2026-10-04 Daniel Motz gave the founder permission to include Query-by-Graph
in Zebratlas and redistribute its built package, including WebAssembly, within
the Zebratlas repository and website. This permission is recorded in project
decision D58; it does not change the upstream All Rights Reserved licence or
grant a general open-source licence. Credit is retained here, in README, and
in the query inspector with a link to Daniel Motz's website.

The original integration pins upstream source without local source changes.
This submission ships the permitted built artifacts and adapters, without upstream Git history.
Zebratlas presentation/model adapters compile against the actual upstream
Vue/Rete editor and Rust WebAssembly converter. Bundled transitive dependency
notices and source links are in web/public/query-by-graph/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
The build manifest records versions and artifact SHA-256 hashes. Those
dependencies retain their own licences; this notice does not supersede them.

Supported SPARQL editing uses Traqula parser/generator 1.4.0 (MIT),
https://github.com/comunica/traqula. Its dependency licence texts and pinned
versions are retained in web/public/query-by-graph/SPARQL-LICENSES.txt.
